.TH KIRISUTE 1 "2026-11-02" "kirisute" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kirisute \- cut Nintendo DS and DSi ROM files down to their real size
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kirisute
.br
.B kirisute
.RI [ options ] " " rom ...
.br
.B kirisute doctor
.br
.B kirisute version
.br
.B kirisute help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kirisute
removes the padding at the end of Nintendo DS and DSi ROM files. Each ROM is
cut to the size its header declares: the used ROM size for a DS ROM, plus its
download-play RSA certificate when it has one, and the full DSi area for a
DSi-enhanced or DSi-only ROM, as GodMode9 trims them.
.PP
A ROM given as a file is trimmed whatever its name. A folder gives the
.I .nds
files directly inside it, and every subfolder too with
.BR \-\-recursive .
Symbolic links, hidden files and hidden folders are left alone, and
.B kirisute
looks no deeper than 32 folders.
.PP
A file whose logo or header checksum is wrong, that is too small to hold a
header, or whose header declares more than the file holds, stays as it is with
a warning. Each trimmed ROM is written to a temporary file beside it, given the
original's permissions and renamed over it, so an interrupted run never leaves
half a file.
.PP
Before a trim,
.B kirisute
prints how many ROMs it found and what it is about to do. Without a ROM on a
terminal it asks for a file or folder, offering the current folder.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
List the tools kirisute needs, with the flavor and version of each. Exits
non-zero only when one is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the platform.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
List what would be trimmed and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Print each ROM's header and change nothing: its title, game code, unit code,
download-play certificate, trimmed size and padding.
.TP
.BR \-\-verify ", " \-\-no\-verify
Trim only a ROM whose padding holds nothing but 00 or FF bytes. A ROM with any
other byte past its real size stays as it is, and the warning names the first
such byte.
.TP
.BR \-\-backup ", " \-\-no\-backup
Keep each original as
.IR rom .bak.
A ROM that already has one stays as it is.
.TP
.B \-\-recursive
Look for
.I .nds
files in every subfolder of each folder given.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as one JSON object on stdout, for scripts: the counts of ROMs
found, read, trimmed, already trimmed, skipped and failed, the bytes saved, and
one entry per file with its status, size, kind and trimmed size.
.PP
.B \-\-
ends the options. A file named help, doctor or version is trimmed by giving
its path, such as
.IR ./help .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KIRISUTE_VERIFY
yes or no, the default for
.BR \-\-verify ,
no unless set.
.TP
.B KIRISUTE_BACKUP
yes or no, the default for
.BR \-\-backup ,
no unless set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every ROM was trimmed or already at its real size. 1 when a file was
skipped or could not be trimmed, or the arguments are wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kirisute \-\-dry\-run *.nds
Show what trimming every ROM in the current folder would do.
.TP
.B kirisute \-\-backup \-\-verify game.nds
Trim one ROM, keep the original, and refuse if the padding holds data.
.TP
.B kirisute \-\-recursive ~/roms/nds
Trim every ROM under a folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR head (1),
.BR od (1)
